<title>FRANCE: U.S. top origin for Jan-Nov 96 Paris air imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top origin for Jan-Nov 96 Paris air imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in January-November 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal countries of origin for ADP imports during the period January-November 1996, with percentage change on January-November 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	137,268 tonnes  up    3.1 pct</p>
<p> 2  India		   26,753 tonnes  up   23.0</p>
<p> 3  Canada		  24,051 tonnes  up    0.9</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	     18,714 tonnes  down  3.1</p>
<p> 5  Japan		   18,525 tonnes  down  7.5</p>
<p> 6  United Kingdom	16,394 tonnes  down  2.5</p>
<p> 7  Germany		 14,071 tonnes  up   30.2</p>
<p> 8  Italy		   11,614 tonnes  up    2.8</p>
<p> 9  Thailand		10,452 tonnes  down 14.8</p>
<p> 10 Kenya		    9,501 tonnes  down  5.9</p>
<p> 11 French West Indies   7,220 tonnes  down  3.6</p>
<p> 12 Senegal		  6,602 tonnes  up   38.8</p>
<p> 13 UAE			6,601 tonnes  down  6.5</p>
<p> 14 Morocco		  6,048 tonnes  down  8.2</p>
<p> 15 Argentina		5,856 tonnes  up   19.2</p>
<p> 16 South Africa	   5,497 tonnes  up   13.5</p>
<p> 17 China		    5,217 tonnes  up    7.1</p>
<p> 18 Brazil		   5,157 tonnes  down 29.6</p>
<p> 19 Singapore		4,964 tonnes  down  0.6</p>
<p> 20 Switzerland	    4,691 tonnes  up    5.4</p>
<p>    Total		  345,196 tonnes</p>
<p>Global January-November 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 475,497 tonnes, an increase of 1.9 percent on the same period last year, ADP said.</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
